  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "# PostgreSQL Slow Query Review",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "7c5dcb78-4bb8-4035-85af-d4b0b57b9dfd"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0002",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "## Context",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "c2c211e5-0c3f-46aa-8f29-9a733a87e54b"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0003",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "This note captures a repeatable way to review slow SQL queries before blindly adding indexes.",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [],
  "evidence_id": "d6003682-aa57-47c0-8e5a-d9c47a3914b2"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0004",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "## Procedure",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "091dce6d-d676-45d0-b26e-4e9b8cee0b9d"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0005",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "1. Capture the worst queries from `pg_stat_statements`.\n2. Run `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and compare the actual plan with the expected access path.\n3. Measure whether the bottleneck is I/O, CPU, or lock contention.",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [],
  "evidence_id": "51848cbe-782a-409f-aa66-6dc38e370820"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0006",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "## Rules",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "ef533090-62ab-4bdb-94af-6fd6186633e6"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0007",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "If the query is I/O bound, review index coverage before rewriting business logic.\nIf row estimates diverge sharply from actual rows, inspect stale statistics.",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [],
  "evidence_id": "ea1c71c4-18e5-4e23-8ce5-94421ea7efc5"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0008",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "## Anti-patterns",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "34efa572-9bd8-4a3e-83a6-d75f64458858"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0009",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "Avoid adding overlapping indexes without calculating write amplification.\nDo not change the query text and the index strategy at the same time.",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [],
  "evidence_id": "e2feaf12-5821-4911-82be-7e40402b8e09"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0010",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "## Verification",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [
    "heading"
  ],
  "evidence_id": "96dd9984-f591-417c-a581-11e3488cbd54"
},
{
  "asset_id": "d7c8c560-c7e3-4b60-9725-d86af8ccea88",
  "span_ref": "paragraph:0011",
  "content_type": "text",
  "content": "Verify the fix by comparing latency, buffer hits, and row estimates before and after the change.",
  "speaker": null,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "tags": [],
  "evidence_id": "233a0a20-86cd-4425-98c9-67db331aa6fa"
}
]
